.TH EMUERA-TTY 1 "2026-10-18" "emuera-tty" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
emuera-tty \- play Emuera (era) games in a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emuera-tty
.RI [ GAME ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B emuera-tty
.I GAME
.BR \-\-saves " | " \-\-backup\-saves
.br
.B emuera-tty
.BR \-\-install " | " \-\-upgrade " | " \-\-uninstall " | " \-\-reset\-data
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B emuera-tty
runs games written for Emuera, the engine of eratohoTW, AnonTW, eraNAS
(pops-tw), eraMegaten and the other era games, in a terminal instead of
the Windows window. It reads the game's
.IR CSV/ ,
.I ERB/
and
.I resources/
folders directly; the
.I Emuera.exe
next to them is not used. Saves are Emuera's own files, so they move both
ways between emuera-tty and Emuera.
.PP
.I GAME
is a game folder (the one holding
.I CSV/
and
.IR ERB/ )
or an archive of one
.RI ( .zip ", " .tar.gz ", " .7z ", ...),"
which is extracted once into the data folder. Without
.IR GAME :
the current folder if it is a game, else the game played last, else a
launcher opens with the game library and a folder browser.
.SH PLAYING
.TP
.B Numbers, Enter, clicks
Choose a menu entry: type its number and press Enter, or click it (a
picture that is a button anywhere on it).
Resting the pointer on a button with a tooltip shows it after half a
second, or the game's delay.
.TP
.B Enter, any key, click
Continue where the game waits
.RB ( "\(dA (Enter)" ).
.TP
.BR "Right click" ", " Tab
Continue and skip the text that follows until the game asks for a choice
(Emuera's message skip). On a choice: pick it and skip after it.
.TP
.BR \(<- ", " \(-> ", " Home ", " End ", " Delete ", " Backspace
Edit the line being typed.
.TP
.BR \en ", " \ee ", " (...)*\fIn\fR " in typed text"
One line answers several inputs, as in Emuera:
.B \en
separates them,
.B \ee
after one skips the text that follows, and
.BI ( ... )* n
repeats:
.B (0\ee\en)*3
answers 0 three times.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-U ", " Esc
Clear the line being typed.
.TP
.BR \(ua ", " \(da
Go through the last 100 inputs, typed or clicked, as in Emuera (one
brought back is selected: typing replaces it). Where the game waits, scroll.
.TP
.BR PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Ctrl+\(ua ", " Ctrl+\(da ", " Alt+\(ua ", " Alt+\(da ", wheel"
Scroll back through earlier text (Home and End too while nothing is
typed); End returns.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-O
The options overlay (also F3, unless a keyboard macro is stored on it): display settings, \fBGame settings\fR (Emuera's
settings window: the game's
.IR emuera.config ,
shared with Emuera.exe), \fBManage saves\fR, switching game, quitting.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-T
Back to the title screen (asks first).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-R
Restart the game (asks first).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-E
Read the ERB files again and carry on with the game as it is (also F5,
unless a keyboard macro is stored on it).
.TP
.BR F1 " ... " F12 ", " Shift+F1 " ... " F12
Keyboard macros, while the game's \fBUse keyboard macros\fR is on (as in
Emuera, the default): Shift+F\fIn\fR stores the line being typed, F\fIn\fR
puts it back (at a wait, gives it at once). Kept in the game's
.IR macro.txt ,
shared with Emuera.exe. With the setting off, the other Fn keys take their
place (F3 and F5 as above).
.TP
.BR Alt+0 " ... " 9
Switch between the ten macro groups (also Ctrl+0...9 where the terminal
reports it).
.TP
.B Esc
Stop a running macro.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-L
Redraw the screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Quit (also while a script is busy). Save first.
.SH CLIPBOARD
With
.B 表示したテキストをクリップボードにコピーする:YES
in
.I emuera.config
(or \fBCopy to clipboard\fR set to \fBon\fR in the overlay), newly printed
lines are put on the clipboard through the terminal (OSC 52) when the game
waits for input, and on WAIT and clicks as the clipboard options in
.I emuera.config
say.
.SH TRANSLATED GAMES
Emuera-Anchor's translation files are read from the game's
.I CSV/
folder:
.IR Abl_TR.csv ", " Talent_TR.csv ", ..."
(\fIoriginal\fB,\fItranslation\fR lines, kept as written after the
original's leading spaces; \fB;\fR starts a comment) translate CSV names
when a script prints them, stores them in a string or returns them with
RETURNF, as in Anchor (conditions, CALL arguments and most built-in
functions see the originals; saves hold the translations; a name with a
fixed index, like \fBTALENTNAME:5\fR, is treated as Anchor treats such
constants),
.I ALL_TR.csv
a whole printed or stored \fB%...%\fR value, and
.I TRCHARA*.csv
the characters' names (blocks from \fBNO,\fIn\fR to \fBENDCHR\fR or
\fBENDCHAR\fR, keys in any case; a field replaces only what the
character's own CSV gives; problems are reported when the game loads).
.B TR_NAME(\fIcode\fB, \fIindex or name\fB)
gives scripts a translated name; an unknown table, or a key that isn't a
name or named index in it, is a script error, as in Anchor.
Lines from a \fB{\fR line to a \fB}\fR line are read as one, as in Anchor.
A \fI_TR.csv\fR line without exactly one comma, a misplaced \fB{\fR or \fB}\fR,
or a name given twice, is reported when the game loads and skipped.
.I PARAM.CSV
is read in place of
.IR PALAM.CSV ,
and in such a game, or one with translation files, scripts may write
\fBPARAM\fR for \fBPALAM\fR, as in Anchor.
.SH MANAGING SAVES
\fBCtrl\-O\fR \(-> \fBManage saves\fR lists the game's saves with their date and
the comment Emuera shows. For one save: copy or move it to another slot,
export it to a file, delete it. For all of them: back up the save folder,
restore a backup, import a save file. A deleted or overwritten save is
always copied to the backups first.
.PP
Saves the game writes are kept the same way: the version a save replaces
goes to the backups as
.IR DATE -auto- NAME
(the last 10 of each file, then one a day for 30 days, one a week for 26
weeks), the first save replaced that emuera-tty didn't write (Emuera.exe's)
as
.IR DATE -original- NAME ,
never thinned. Each save is written to a temporary file, flushed, read
back and checked before it replaces the old one, and logged in
.I save-log.tsv
with the emuera-tty version and commit that wrote it.
.TP
.B \-\-saves
List the saves of
.I GAME
(slot, date, size, comment) and say how many backups there are.
.TP
.B \-\-backup\-saves
Copy all of
.IR GAME 's
saves into a new, dated backup folder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-choose
Open the launcher even if a game is remembered.
.TP
.BR \-\-gfx " auto|kitty|iterm|sixel|fb|none"
How pictures are drawn. \fBauto\fR (default) asks the terminal: kitty
graphics (kitty, Ghostty, Konsole), iTerm2 inline images (iTerm2, WezTerm), sixel
(foot, xterm \-ti vt340, mlterm, Windows Terminal), or the Linux
framebuffer on the console. \fBnone\fR shows placeholders.
Inside tmux, kitty graphics go through tmux's passthrough as Unicode
placeholders, which needs \fBset \-g allow\-passthrough all\fR in the
tmux configuration (\fBon\fR loses pictures sent while the pane is hidden); GNU screen shows no pictures.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Plain line-by-line stdin/stdout, for scripts and tests; waits continue at
once and the end of input quits.
.TP
.B \-\-echo
Echo the inputs in headless mode.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Load the game, compile every function, report parse errors (also, as in
Emuera, statements a \fB#FUNCTION\fR may not use) and exit.
(Otherwise a function is compiled when it first runs, and its errors are
reported then.)
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Commands emuera-tty doesn't implement are errors instead of warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Run
.B [IF_DEBUG]
blocks and
.B ;#;
lines, like Emuera's debug mode. \fBRestart in debug mode\fR in the
options overlay restarts the game with it (and \fBRestart without debug
mode\fR without it).
.SS Retro and serial terminals
.TP
.BR \-\-retro [ =line ]
Drive the terminal through its terminfo entry with ASCII output only: box
drawing from the alternate character set, kana romanised. Automatic when
.B $TERM
isn't an ANSI terminal (vt52, adm3a, dumb, ...).
.B =line
prints line by line for terminals without cursor addressing.
.TP
.BI \-\-term " NAME"
The terminfo name of the terminal (default
.BR $TERM ;
vt100 with
.BR \-\-serial ).
.TP
.BI \-\-serial " DEVICE"
Play on a terminal on a serial line
.RI ( /dev/ttyS0 ", " /dev/ttyUSB0 ,
or
.I COM3
on Windows).
.TP
.BI \-\-baud " N"
Line speed (default 9600).
.TP
.BI \-\-serial\-format " 8N1|7E1|..."
Data bits, parity and stop bits (default 8N1).
.TP
.BR \-\-flow " xon|rts|none"
Flow control (default xon).
.TP
.BI \-\-size " COLSxROWS"
The screen size when the terminal can't report it.
.SS Setup
.TP
.B \-\-install
Copy this program into a folder on your PATH, and this page into the
matching
.IR share/man/man1 .
.TP
.B \-\-upgrade
Fetch the latest source with git, build it with cargo and install it.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Remove the installed copy and this page.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-data
Forget emuera-tty's settings and game library. Saves are not touched.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Short help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EMUERA_GFX
Default for
.BR \-\-gfx .
.TP
.B EMUERA_COLORS
.BR truecolor ", " 256 " or " 16 :
the colour depth, when detection guesses wrong.
.TP
.B EMUERA_AMBIGUOUS
.BR wide ", " narrow ", " single " or " osc66 :
how box drawing and symbols get Emuera's two columns.
.TP
.B EMUERA_MEASURE=0
Skip measuring how wide the terminal draws ambiguous characters.
.TP
.B EMUERA_MOUSE
.BR off " / " term :
no console mouse;
.BR mice :
read
.I /dev/input/mice
even outside the Linux console.
.TP
.BR EMUERA_SAVE_HISTORY= 0
Keep no history of replaced saves and no save log (saves are still
written safely).
.TP
.BR EMUERA_SOUND= on|off
Play the game's sounds (default: yes, except over SSH).
.TP
.BI EMUERA_SOUND_PLAYER= name
The player program for sounds:
.BR mpv ", " ffplay ", " mplayer ", " afplay ", " pw-play ", " paplay ", " aplay " or " powershell
(default: the first of these found). MIDI files play through
.B fluidsynth
found in
.B PATH
(Linux packages; on Windows the release zip's
.I bin
folder added to
.BR PATH ;
on macOS Homebrew), with the game's
.I soundfont.sf2
if it has one, else on Linux the system's. In a game that comes with eraMidi
.RI ( eramidi.exe ,
as eratohoReverse), a printed song title after a \[u266A] plays
.IR media/reverse/ title .mid
as eraMidi would.
.TP
.BI EMUERA_TRANSLATE_CMD= command
For
.IR "Translate to" :
a command that reads a line of dialog on stdin and prints its
translation (instead of Ollama, LibreTranslate, translateLocally or
argos-translate).
.TP
.BI EMUERA_TRANSLATE_LOG= file
Append every new translation to
.IR file :
the script file and line that printed it, the languages, the original
and the translation, separated by tabs. A line translated by a middle
click that can't be traced to its script file has
\fB(force-translated, cannot trace original file)\fR instead.
.TP
.B DEEPL_AUTH_KEY
A DeepL API key for the
.B deepl
translator (without one it uses DeepL's free keyless endpoint).
.TP
.BI EMUERA_TRANSLATE_MODEL= name
The Ollama or translateLocally model for
.IR "Translate to" .
.TP
.B EMUERA_LIST_BUTTONS=1
With
.BR \-\-headless ,
print the values of the buttons on screen before each input.
.TP
.B EMUERA_THREADS
Cap the threads used for loading and picture decoding.
.TP
.B EMUERA_SEED
Fix the random number generator (reproducible runs).
.TP
.BI EMUERA_TRACE= name
Log calls to functions whose name contains
.IR name ,
with timestamps, to stderr.
.TP
.BI EMUERA_PROFILE= file
Sample which ERB function runs every millisecond and keep
.I file
updated with the totals and the input the script waits for.
.TP
.BR EMUERA_INJECT= "STMT||STMT, " EMUERA_INJECT_AT= n
Run those statements just before the
.IR n -th
input (debugging).
.TP
.B EMUERA_TIMING=1
Print how long loading takes, and the memory in use after each phase.
.TP
.B EMUERA_PARSE=all
Compile every function at load instead of on its first call (more memory,
all parse errors at once).
.TP
.BI EMUERA_CODE_MB= n
Compiled functions may take about
.I n
MB (default: a sixteenth of the machine's memory); beyond that, those
called longest ago are dropped and compiled again when needed.
.TP
.BI EMUERA_GBUF_MB= n
Graphics buffers may take
.I n
MB unpacked (default: an eighth of the memory); the least recently used
are packed until used again.
.TP
.BI EMUERA_MEMSTATS= file
Write what the memory holds to
.I file
at every input.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME
Where settings and data go (below).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/emuera-tty/config
Settings and the game library
.RB ( %APPDATA%\eemuera-tty
on Windows).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/emuera-tty/games/
Games extracted from archives.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/emuera-tty/backups/GAME/
Save backups, one dated folder each, and the save history with its log,
.IR save-log.tsv .
.TP
.IR GAME /sav/save NN .sav ", " GAME /sav/global.sav
The game's saves (next to the game when its
.I emuera.config
doesn't ask for a
.I sav
folder), in Emuera's binary format: an Emuera save loaded and saved again
comes out byte for byte as Emuera writes it.
.TP
.IR GAME /emuera.config
Emuera's configuration; font size, line height, colours, PRINTC widths,
save options and the ERB folder options (search subfolders, sort by file
name, which set the load order as in Emuera) are honoured.
.TP
.IR GAME /macro.txt
The keyboard macros, in Emuera's format (written on quitting when one was
stored).
.SH NOTES
Developed and tested on Linux. macOS, the BSDs, Windows, Termux (Android)
and the other systems are compile-checked only and untested. Small boards
such as the Raspberry Pi Zero (512 MB) have enough memory for big games;
the ARM builds are tried under emulation only, as are those for RISC-V,
PowerPC (both byte orders) and LoongArch; MIPS, SPARC, s390x, m68k and
others are compile-checked. Saves are the same files on every CPU.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR terminfo (5),
.BR kitty (1),
.BR foot (1)
.PP
https://github.com/astartes-gaming/emuera-tty
